WEBVTT

00:00:00.118 --> 00:00:02.084
Press Tab. The menu won't open.

00:00:03.125 --> 00:00:04.994
Turn on the Curb Cut Chrome extension.

00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:07.288
Same keys. Now the menu opens.

00:00:08.642 --> 00:00:11.017
For millions of people, this is the web.

00:00:11.017 --> 00:00:13.167
Menus that only work with a mouse.

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:14.667
Buttons with no name.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:15.869
Text too faint to read.

00:00:16.034 --> 00:00:21.077
95.9 percent of the top million
home pages have barriers like these.

00:00:22.136 --> 00:00:24.236
Websites take years to fix them.

00:00:24.236 --> 00:00:26.245
The people shut out can't wait that long.

00:00:27.621 --> 00:00:30.238
Curb Cut fixes them now,
right in your browser.

00:00:31.621 --> 00:00:33.946
A screen reader used to say just, button.

00:00:33.946 --> 00:00:35.584
Now it says, previous slide.

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:38.041
Faint text, made readable.

00:00:39.642 --> 00:00:41.692
And no fix ships on a guess.

00:00:41.692 --> 00:00:46.142
Kane, an AI tester, tries the task
the way a disabled person would.

00:00:46.142 --> 00:00:47.917
Without the fix, it fails.

00:00:47.917 --> 00:00:49.567
With the fix, it passes.

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:50.919
That recording is the proof.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.036
105 fixes are live today,
and every one shows its proof.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:01.725
On sites we've never seen, Jev names
unlabelled buttons in about a second.

00:01:01.725 --> 00:01:03.644
When it isn't sure, it stays quiet.

00:01:04.614 --> 00:01:08.168
Then the fix goes to the site owner,
so one day, nobody needs us.

00:01:09.121 --> 00:01:11.932
Curb Cut. Fixing the web
for the people it shuts out.

00:01:12.074 --> 00:01:13.409
Get Curb Cut for Chrome.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.760
Developers can do the same thing
on a site they're building.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.776
Start with what a visitor came to do.

00:01:21.196 --> 00:01:26.103
Here, someone wants to find a pair of headphones
and add them to their cart using a keyboard.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.880
Give that task and the
address to curbcut check.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.825
Kane opens the shop and tries it.

00:01:32.245 --> 00:01:33.480
Watch the Add button.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.240
The keyboard skips right past it.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.056
The headphones stay on the shelf.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.580
Curb Cut proposes a small change.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:43.656
Let the button take focus,
and let Enter activate it.

00:01:44.076 --> 00:01:45.360
Kane tries again.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.160
Same shop, same headphones, same keyboard.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:50.070
This time there's an item in the cart.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.140
A developer can put that
check into Claude Code, too.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.276
Here it runs when Claude tries to finish.

00:01:56.696 --> 00:01:59.410
The first time, the button
still skips the keyboard.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:02.371
The check fails and the Stop
hook sends the work back.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.560
The developer fixes the
button in the site itself.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.136
Claude reaches the end again.

00:02:08.556 --> 00:02:10.720
This time Kane can add the headphones.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.823
The check passes and Claude can finish.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:18.040
A person using the extension
can look at the evidence, too.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:20.769
Open Curb Cut on the page
and choose the recording.

00:02:21.189 --> 00:02:23.320
It shows what happened in the browser.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.732
You can see for yourself
whether the menu opened.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:30.160
On a new page, Jev looks
at what each button does.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.800
Here on Meridiano, one opens the menu.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.153
Another opens search.

00:02:34.573 --> 00:02:36.480
People checked the suggestions.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.840
Jev got 13 right out of 15.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.101
When it's unsure,
it leaves the button alone.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:45.600
If something else gets in the
way, open Report a barrier.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.492
Describe what you were trying
to do and where you got stuck.

00:02:48.912 --> 00:02:51.481
The extension keeps a
draft so you can review it.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:56.600
And when a site owner makes a repair,
the browser should get out of the way.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:00.037
Kane tries the task with the
extension's fix switched off.

00:03:00.457 --> 00:03:01.960
The button works on its own.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:03.737
Curb Cut retires the fix.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:09.828
The next person who comes to buy those
headphones can use the keyboard from the start.
